ent framework; expert review required", "source_url": "https://doi.org/10.3390/nu13051401", "review_note": "Keep this item flagged for expert review before public release. It translates evidence and/or teen lived experience into self-management content."}}, "choices": [], "feedback": {"answer_type": "MYTH", "summary": "Independence means building your own decision-making and self-advocacy skills. It does not mean refusing help. Asking a friend, parent, server, teacher or healthcare professional for useful information can be part of managing celiac independently."}, "teaching_point": "Independent does not mean alone.", "next_step": null, "related_content_ids": [], "xp_value": 5, "source_type": "EDITORIAL", "source_organization": "Meyer & Naveh self-management framework; expert review required", "source_title": null, "source_url": "https://doi.org/10.3390/nu13051401", "author": null, "review_status": "IN_REVIEW", "expert_reviewer": null, "medical_review_required": false, "content_version": 1, "last_reviewed": null, "active": true}, {"content_id": "8f2b4509-1454-53ae-a365-5898100f3154", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "title": "Sometimes I can participate in a social event even if I decide not to eat there.", "subtitle": null, "domain": "LIVE", "topic": "Belonging", "interaction_type": "CHOICE", "difficulty": null, "estimated_minutes": null, "intro": null, "content_body": {"format": "myth_or_fact_v1", "content_id": "MOF_020", "domains": ["LIVE", "TRUST"], "original_metadata": {"content_id": "MOF_020", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "statement": "Sometimes I can participate in a social event even if I decide not to eat there.", "answer_type": "IT_DEPENDS", "domain": "LIVE, TRUST", "topic": "Belonging", "xp_value": "+5", "review_status": "expert_review", "expert_reviewed": "false", "medical_review_required": "false", "content_version": "1.0", "active": "true", "explanation": "Sometimes eating is central to the event; other times the social connection matters most. Eating beforehand, bringing a backup, or simply joining friends without eating may be reasonable options depending on the situation.", "takeaway": "Participation does not always have to depend on eating.", "source_organization": "Teen lived-experience synthesis; expert review required", "source_url": null, "review_note": "Keep this item flagged for expert review before public release. It translates evidence and/or teen lived experience into self-management content."}}, "choices": [], "feedback": {"answer_type": "IT_DEPENDS", "summary": "Sometimes eating is central to the event; other times the social connection matters most. Eating beforehand, bringing a backup, or simply joining friends without eating may be reasonable options depending on the situation."}, "teaching_point": "Participation does not always have to depend on eating.", "next_step": null, "related_content_ids": [], "xp_value": 5, "source_type": "EDITORIAL", "source_organization": "Teen lived-experience synthesis; expert review required", "source_title": null, "source_url": null, "author": null, "review_status": "IN_REVIEW", "expert_reviewer": null, "medical_review_required": false, "content_version": 1, "last_reviewed": null, "active": true}, {"content_id": "01bfc669-5cdc-5803-8124-8d5a91d7855d", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "title": "If everyone tells me a food is fine, that is the same as having enough information to decide for myself.", "subtitle": null, "domain": "TRUST", "topic": "Decision-Making", "interaction_type": "CHOICE", "difficulty": null, "estimated_minutes": null, "intro": null, "content_body": {"format": "myth_or_fact_v1", "content_id": "MOF_021", "domains": ["TRUST"], "original_metadata": {"content_id": "MOF_021", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "statement": "If everyone tells me a food is fine, that is the same as having enough information to decide for myself.", "answer_type": "MYTH", "domain": "TRUST", "topic": "Decision-Making", "xp_value": "+5", "review_status": "expert_review", "expert_reviewed": "false", "medical_review_required": "false", "content_version": "1.0", "active": "true", "explanation": "Reassurance can feel helpful, but it may not answer questions about ingredients, preparation or cross-contact. You can decide what information you need.", "takeaway": "Reassurance and information are not the same thing.", "source_organization": "Beyond Celiac cross-contact guidance + teen lived-experience extension", "source_url": "https://www.beyondceliac.org/gluten-free-diet/cross-contact/", "review_note": "Keep this item flagged for expert review before public release. It translates evidence and/or teen lived experience into self-management content."}}, "choices": [], "feedback": {"answer_type": "MYTH", "summary": "Reassurance can feel helpful, but it may not answer questions about ingredients, preparation or cross-contact. You can decide what information you need."}, "teaching_point": "Reassurance and information are not the same thing.", "next_step": null, "related_content_ids": [], "xp_value": 5, "source_type": "EDITORIAL", "source_organization": "Beyond Celiac cross-contact guidance + teen lived-experience extension", "source_title": null, "source_url": "https://www.beyondceliac.org/gluten-free-diet/cross-contact/", "author": null, "review_status": "IN_REVIEW", "expert_reviewer": null, "medical_review_required": false, "content_version": 1, "last_reviewed": null, "active": true}, {"content_id": "9e81d065-0aa6-5a83-aef2-7d3b6cc4bfa4", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "title": "If I've asked all the right questions and still feel nervous, I have to eat the food anyway or I'm letting celiac win.", "subtitle": null, "domain": "TRUST", "topic": "Confidence", "interaction_type": "CHOICE", "difficulty": null, "estimated_minutes": null, "intro": null, "content_body": {"format": "myth_or_fact_v1", "content_id": "MOF_022", "domains": ["TRUST", "LIVE"], "original_metadata": {"content_id": "MOF_022", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "statement": "If I've asked all the right questions and still feel nervous, I have to eat the food anyway or I'm letting celiac win.", "answer_type": "MYTH", "domain": "TRUST, LIVE", "topic": "Confidence", "xp_value": "+5", "review_status": "clinical_review", "expert_reviewed": "false", "medical_review_required": "true", "content_version": "1.0", "active": "true", "explanation": "My C-Day should never pressure you to eat. You can notice whether information is still missing, whether you are feeling uncertain, or whether you simply prefer another option.", "takeaway": "Confidence is not measured by forcing yourself to eat.", "source_organization": "Teen lived-experience synthesis; expert/clinical review required", "source_url": null, "review_note": "Keep this item flagged for expert review before public release. It translates evidence and/or teen lived experience into self-management content.", "clinical_review_note": "This card touches emotional adjustment or food-related distress. Do not diagnose, pathologize, or pressure eating behavior."}}, "choices": [], "feedback": {"answer_type": "MYTH", "summary": "My C-Day should never pressure you to eat. You can notice whether information is still missing, whether you are feeling uncertain, or whether you simply prefer another option."}, "teaching_point": "Confidence is not measured by forcing yourself to eat.", "next_step": null, "related_content_ids": [], "xp_value": 5, "source_type": "EDITORIAL", "source_organization": "Teen lived-experience synthesis; expert/clinical review required", "source_title": null, "source_url": null, "author": null, "review_status": "IN_REVIEW", "expert_reviewer": null, "medical_review_required": true, "content_version": 1, "last_reviewed": null, "active": true}, {"content_id": "0aa4a5bc-8e89-5f29-828a-35fdffc3641a", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "title": "It's possible for foods I used to love to feel completely different after a celiac diagnosis.", "subtitle": null, "domain": "TRUST", "topic": "Adjustment", "interaction_type": "CHOICE", "difficulty": null, "estimated_minutes": null, "intro": null, "content_body": {"format": "myth_or_fact_v1", "content_id": "MOF_023", "domains": ["TRUST", "LIVE"], "original_metadata": {"content_id": "MOF_023", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "statement": "It's possible for foods I used to love to feel completely different after a celiac diagnosis.", "answer_type": "LETS_RETHINK_IT", "domain": "TRUST, LIVE", "topic": "Adjustment", "xp_value": "+5", "review_status": "clinical_review", "expert_reviewed": "false", "medical_review_required": "true", "content_version": "1.0", "active": "true", "explanation": "A major dietary and health change can change how someone thinks or feels about food. My C-Day does not label that reaction as good or bad. If food-related fear or avoidance is causing significant distress or limiting eating, support from a caregiver and celiac healthcare team may be helpful.", "takeaway": "Adjustment can be emotional as well as practical.", "source_organization": "Teen lived-experience synthesis; clinical review required", "source_url": null, "review_note": "Keep this item flagged for expert review before public release. It translates evidence and/or teen lived experience into self-management content.", "clinical_review_note": "This card touches emotional adjustment or food-related distress. Do not diagnose, pathologize, or pressure eating behavior."}}, "choices": [], "feedback": {"answer_type": "LETS_RETHINK_IT", "summary": "A major dietary and health change can change how someone thinks or feels about food. My C-Day does not label that reaction as good or bad. If food-related fear or avoidance is causing significant distress or limiting eating, support from a caregiver and celiac healthcare team may be helpful."}, "teaching_point": "Adjustment can be emotional as well as practical.", "next_step": null, "related_content_ids": [], "xp_value": 5, "source_type": "EDITORIAL", "source_organization": "Teen lived-experience synthesis; clinical review required", "source_title": null, "source_url": null, "author": null, "review_status": "IN_REVIEW", "expert_reviewer": null, "medical_review_required": true, "content_version": 1, "last_reviewed": null, "active": true}, {"content_id": "6277a92a-42bc-528d-aee3-1da664079f64", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "title": "If I'm tired of researching, checking and explaining, it means I'm bad at managing celiac.", "subtitle": null, "domain": "LIVE", "topic": "Planning Fatigue", "interaction_type": "CHOICE", "difficulty": null, "estimated_minutes": null, "intro": null, "content_body": {"format": "myth_or_fact_v1", "content_id": "MOF_024", "domains": ["LIVE", "MANAGE"], "original_metadata": {"content_id": "MOF_024", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "statement": "If I'm tired of researching, checking and explaining, it means I'm bad at managing celiac.", "answer_type": "MYTH", "domain": "LIVE, MANAGE", "topic": "Planning Fatigue", "xp_value": "+5", "review_status": "expert_review", "expert_reviewed": "false", "medical_review_required": "false", "content_version": "1.0", "active": "true", "explanation": "Knowing how to manage celiac does not mean the work never feels tiring. Using familiar options, sharing planning with others, or choosing a lower-effort strategy can sometimes reduce the mental load.", "takeaway": "Planning fatigue is different from not knowing what to do.", "source_organization": "Teen lived-experience synthesis; expert review required", "source_url": null, "review_note": "Keep this item flagged for expert review before public release. It translates evidence and/or teen lived experience into self-management content."}}, "choices": [], "feedback": {"answer_type": "MYTH", "summary": "Knowing how to manage celiac does not mean the work never feels tiring. Using familiar options, sharing planning with others, or choosing a lower-effort strategy can sometimes reduce the mental load."}, "teaching_point": "Planning fatigue is different from not knowing what to do.", "next_step": null, "related_content_ids": [], "xp_value": 5, "source_type": "EDITORIAL", "source_organization": "Teen lived-experience synthesis; expert review required", "source_title": null, "source_url": null, "author": null, "review_status": "IN_REVIEW", "expert_reviewer": null, "medical_review_required": false, "content_version": 1, "last_reviewed": null, "active": true}, {"content_id": "1c9db81f-3bfc-5eb2-b5d7-454efce57e27", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "title": "Having celiac means I should always be the person teaching everyone else about it.", "subtitle": null, "domain": "LEAD", "topic": "Advocacy", "interaction_type": "CHOICE", "difficulty": null, "estimated_minutes": null, "intro": null, "content_body": {"format": "myth_or_fact_v1", "content_id": "MOF_025", "domains": ["LEAD", "SPEAK"], "original_metadata": {"content_id": "MOF_025", "content_type": "MYTH_OR_FACT", "statement": "Having celiac means I should always be the person teaching everyone else about it.", "answer_type": "MYTH", "domain": "LEAD, SPEAK", "topic": "Advocacy", "xp_value": "+5", "review_status": "expert_review", "expert_reviewed": "false", "medical_review_required": "false", "content_version": "1.0", "active": "true", "explanation": "You can advocate when you want to, but having celiac does not make educating everyone your responsibility. Sometimes you may explain, share a resource, correct a misconception, or simply move on.", "takeaway": "Advocacy is an option, not another obligation.", "source_organization": "Teen self-management content; expert review required", "source_url": null, "review_note": "Keep this item flagged for expert review before public release. It translates evidence and/or teen lived experience into self-management content."}}, "choices": [], "feedback": {"answer_type": "MYTH", "summary": "You can advocate when you want to, but having celiac does not make educating everyone your responsibility. Sometimes you may explain, share a resource, correct a misconception, or simply move on."}, "teaching_point": "Advocacy is an option, not another obligation.", "next_step": null, "related_content_ids": [], "xp_value": 5, "source_type": "EDITORIAL", "source_organization": "Teen self-management content; expert review required", "source_title": null, "source_url": null, "author": null, "review_status": "IN_REVIEW", "expert_reviewer": null, "medical_review_required": false, "content_version": 1, "last_reviewed": null, "active": true}]$expected$::jsonb)
), checked as (
 select x.record->'content_body'->>'content_id' as card_id,e.content_id,
 not exists(select 1 from jsonb_each(x.record) f where to_jsonb(e)->f.key is distinct from f.value) as matches
 from expected x left join public.explore_content e
 on e.content_id::text=x.record->>'content_id' or e.content_body->>'content_id'=x.record->'content_body'->>'content_id'
)
select card_id,count(content_id) as record_count,
 case when count(content_id)=1 and bool_and(matches) then 'PASS' else 'CHECK MISSING, DUPLICATE, OR CHANGED FIELDS' end as qa_result
from checked group by card_id order by card_id;
